window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-027.json",{"day":27,"title":"Designing a Workshop That People Can Use","targetWords":[{"word":"inhibit","gloss":"妨碍","context":"A participant's experience could show why a design that seemed efficient might inhibit someone with limited movement.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"ventilate","gloss":"通风","context":"The college needed to ventilate the rooms properly and accustom beginners to safe habits.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"withhold","gloss":"不提供","context":"A workshop should neither withhold useful guidance nor make perfection the price of belonging to the group.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"escalate","gloss":"升级","context":"During the trial, organizers watched whether minor problems would escalate.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"excite","gloss":"使兴奋","context":"A loud machine could excite one child and frighten another; a strange sound might signal a fault.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"lubricate","gloss":"润滑","context":"Instructors would show how to lubricate a stiff hinge, fill a small gap, and clean a workbench before starting another job.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"rejoice","gloss":"高兴","context":"They could rejoice in higher participation while admitting that some barriers remained.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"tyre","gloss":"轮胎","context":"A bicycle tyre provided a useful first lesson because its function was familiar even if its construction was not.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"accustom","gloss":"使习惯","context":"The college needed to ventilate the rooms properly and accustom beginners to safe habits.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"inflict","gloss":"造成","context":"Designers took care not to let heavy tools inflict strain or a narrow passage paralyze activity.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"maneuver","gloss":"复杂移动","context":"A visitor could move between stations without attempting a difficult maneuver.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"paralyze","gloss":"使停滞","context":"Designers took care not to let heavy tools inflict strain or a narrow passage paralyze activity.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"should","gloss":"应该","context":"Their approach was to prepare the space for real users, not to assume that users should adapt themselves to whatever space professionals preferred.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"would","gloss":"会","context":"They asked people where they live, what they need, and what would make them willing to return.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"like","gloss":"像；喜欢","context":"One instructor worried that assistance would seem like favoritism; another thought staff must bear responsibility for reducing unnecessary risk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"need","gloss":"需要","context":"They asked people where they live, what they need, and what would make them willing to return.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"live","gloss":"住","context":"They asked people where they live, what they need, and what would make them willing to return.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"must","gloss":"必须","context":"One instructor worried that assistance would seem like favoritism; another thought staff must bear responsibility for reducing unnecessary risk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"show","gloss":"展示","context":"A participant's experience could show why a design that seemed efficient might inhibit someone with limited movement.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"research","gloss":"研究","context":"The research team tried to translate these accounts into practical requirements.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"point","gloss":"要点","context":"The point was to help participants realize that skill can develop through practice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"correspond","gloss":"相符合","context":"Safety instructions had to correspond to the actual layout rather than exist as a document stored elsewhere.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"might","gloss":"可能","context":"A participant's experience could show why a design that seemed efficient might inhibit someone with limited movement.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"seem","gloss":"似乎","context":"One instructor worried that assistance would seem like favoritism; another thought staff must bear responsibility for reducing unnecessary risk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"sentence","gloss":"句子","context":"Another pointed to a sentence on the entrance sign whose meaning was unclear.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"experience","gloss":"经历","context":"A participant's experience could show why a design that seemed efficient might inhibit someone with limited movement.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"care","gloss":"关心","context":"Designers took care not to let heavy tools inflict strain or a narrow passage paralyze activity.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"move","gloss":"移动","context":"A visitor could move between stations without attempting a difficult maneuver.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"remain","gloss":"保持","context":"They had to search for evidence, agree on limits, and remain willing to change a procedure.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"design","gloss":"设计","context":"A participant's experience could show why a design that seemed efficient might inhibit someone with limited movement.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"risk","gloss":"风险","context":"One instructor worried that assistance would seem like favoritism; another thought staff must bear responsibility for reducing unnecessary risk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"fill","gloss":"填","context":"Instructors would show how to lubricate a stiff hinge, fill a small gap, and clean a workbench before starting another job.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"interview","gloss":"采访","context":"When a community college planned a repair workshop, its researchers began with an interview rather than a blueprint.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"sign","gloss":"标牌","context":"Another pointed to a sentence on the entrance sign whose meaning was unclear.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"sound","gloss":"声音","context":"A loud machine could excite one child and frighten another; a strange sound might signal a fault.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"translate","gloss":"转化","context":"The research team tried to translate these accounts into practical requirements.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bear","gloss":"承担","context":"One instructor worried that assistance would seem like favoritism; another thought staff must bear responsibility for reducing unnecessary risk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"approach","gloss":"方法","context":"Their approach was to prepare the space for real users, not to assume that users should adapt themselves to whatever space professionals preferred.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"exist","gloss":"存在","context":"Safety instructions had to correspond to the actual layout rather than exist as a document stored elsewhere.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"agree","gloss":"同意","context":"They had to search for evidence, agree on limits, and remain willing to change a procedure.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"solve","gloss":"解答","context":"The coordinator helped them solve the disagreement by separating access from reward.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"search","gloss":"寻找","context":"They had to search for evidence, agree on limits, and remain willing to change a procedure.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"serve","gloss":"服务","context":"A ramp could serve everyone without deciding whose finished work deserved praise.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"prepare","gloss":"准备","context":"Their approach was to prepare the space for real users, not to assume that users should adapt themselves to whatever space professionals preferred.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"publish","gloss":"公布","context":"At the end of the term, instructors chose to publish the findings, including failures.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"suffer","gloss":"遭受","context":"Beginners might suffer embarrassment if errors were announced aloud, so teachers would treat mistakes as information.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"realize","gloss":"认识到","context":"The point was to help participants realize that skill can develop through practice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"clean","gloss":"清理","context":"Instructors would show how to lubricate a stiff hinge, fill a small gap, and clean a workbench before starting another job.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"reward","gloss":"奖励","context":"The coordinator helped them solve the disagreement by separating access from reward.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"treat","gloss":"对待","context":"Beginners might suffer embarrassment if errors were announced aloud, so teachers would treat mistakes as information.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When a community college planned a repair workshop, its researchers began with an interview rather than a blueprint. They asked people where they live, what they need, and what would make them willing to return. A participant's experience could show why a design that seemed efficient might inhibit someone with limited movement. Another pointed to a sentence on the entrance sign whose meaning was unclear. The research team tried to translate these accounts into practical requirements. Their approach was to prepare the space for real users, not to assume that users should adapt themselves to whatever space professionals preferred.","zh":"社区学院规划维修工坊时，研究者先做访谈，而不是画蓝图。他们询问人们住在哪里、需要什么，以及什么会让人愿意回来。参与者的经历能说明，看似高效的设计为何可能妨碍行动不便者。另一个人指出入口标牌上一句话意思不清。研究团队把这些描述转化为实际要求，让空间适应真实使用者，而不假设使用者理应适应专业人员喜欢的空间。"},{"en":"The college needed to ventilate the rooms properly and accustom beginners to safe habits. Instructors would show how to lubricate a stiff hinge, fill a small gap, and clean a workbench before starting another job. A bicycle tyre provided a useful first lesson because its function was familiar even if its construction was not. A visitor could move between stations without attempting a difficult maneuver. Designers took care not to let heavy tools inflict strain or a narrow passage paralyze activity. Safety instructions had to correspond to the actual layout rather than exist as a document stored elsewhere.","zh":"学院必须保证房间通风，让初学者养成安全习惯。教师演示如何润滑卡住的铰链、填补小缝和开始下一项工作前清理台面。自行车轮胎适合作为第一课，因为即使结构陌生，功能也熟悉。游客无需复杂移动就能在工作台间通行。设计者注意避免重工具造成身体负担，或狭窄通道让活动停滞。安全说明必须对应实际布局，而不是仅作为存放在别处的文件存在。"},{"en":"Not everyone agreed about how much support to provide. One instructor worried that assistance would seem like favoritism; another thought staff must bear responsibility for reducing unnecessary risk. The coordinator helped them solve the disagreement by separating access from reward. A ramp could serve everyone without deciding whose finished work deserved praise. Beginners might suffer embarrassment if errors were announced aloud, so teachers would treat mistakes as information. The point was to help participants realize that skill can develop through practice. A workshop should neither withhold useful guidance nor make perfection the price of belonging to the group.","zh":"并非所有人都同意应提供多少支持。一名教师担心协助显得偏心，另一人认为员工必须承担降低不必要风险的责任。协调者通过区分参与条件与奖励解决分歧：坡道服务每个人，并不决定谁的成品值得赞扬。如果错误被大声宣布，初学者可能难堪，所以教师把错误当作信息来处理。目标是帮助参与者明白，技能可以靠练习发展。工坊既不该隐瞒有用指导，也不应让完美成为融入群体的门槛。"},{"en":"During the trial, organizers watched whether minor problems would escalate. A loud machine could excite one child and frighten another; a strange sound might signal a fault. Staff could not simply like an attractive idea and ignore its consequences. They had to search for evidence, agree on limits, and remain willing to change a procedure. A quiet corner allowed anxious participants to pause without leaving altogether. These arrangements did not remove every difficulty, but they showed care in a concrete form. The college learned that inclusive environments depend as much on ordinary working decisions as on public declarations of welcome.","zh":"试运行时，组织者观察小问题是否升级。吵闹机器可能让一个孩子兴奋、另一个害怕；异常声响可能意味着故障。员工不能只因为喜欢一个好看的想法就忽视后果。他们必须寻找证据、商定边界，并保持改变流程的意愿。安静角落让焦虑的参与者可以暂停，而无需彻底离开。这些安排没有消除所有困难，却具体体现了关怀。学院认识到，包容环境既依靠公开欢迎，也同样依靠日常工作中的决定。"},{"en":"At the end of the term, instructors chose to publish the findings, including failures. They could rejoice in higher participation while admitting that some barriers remained. Their report avoided claiming a universal solution; instead, it offered questions that other institutions could use. Who can reach the tools? Who understands the signs? Who feels able to ask for help? Answers must come from observation as well as professional opinion. A useful public workshop is not merely a room full of equipment. It is a place where people can learn together without having to hide the difficulties that initially brought them there.","zh":"学期结束时，教师决定公布包括失败在内的发现。他们为参与增加而高兴，同时承认仍有障碍。报告没有声称存在普遍解法，而提供其他机构可用的问题：谁能拿到工具？谁看得懂标牌？谁敢求助？答案必须来自观察，也来自专业意见。实用的公共工坊不仅是装满设备的房间，更是一个人们能共同学习、不必隐藏最初使他们来到这里的困难的地方。"}],"previous":26,"next":28});
